-<section><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1.5rem 0"><p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:680px;line-height:1.75">North Myrtle Beach, including communities like Cherry Grove and Ocean Drive, is known for a quieter, family oriented feel than the central strip while still drawing steady vacation-rental demand. Beach proximate inventory here tends toward established, well kept properties.</p></div></section>
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common Questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do you need a permit to short-term rental in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">No separate permit. The city requires a business license for every short-term rental, renewed each year. The owner also collects and pays the accommodations taxes. There is no rental permit, inspection or local-agent rule.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can an out-of-state owner run an Airbnb in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes. The city does not require a local agent or a local manager. The owner lists an emergency contact on the business license application.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What are the neighborhoods in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">The city formed in 1968 from four communities still used as area names: Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach, and Windy Hill, plus resort communities like Barefoot Resort.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What are property taxes on a second home in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In North Myrtle Beach that makes a second home's bill about 3 times a primary home's on the same house.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Which schools serve North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Public schools fall within the North Myrtle Beach attendance area of Horry County Schools. Chapter3 will confirm the exact assignment for an address on the district boundary map.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is North Myrtle Beach better for families?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">It is known for a quieter, family oriented feel than central Myrtle Beach while still offering steady vacation-rental demand.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How is vacation-rental demand in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Established and steady, particularly in beach proximate communities like Cherry Grove and Ocean Drive.</p></div></div></section>
