-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><use href="#c3r-main-street-shopping" x="-7.4" y="-7.4" width="14.7" height="14.7" color="#1c2028"/><text class="l" x="15" y="-3"><tspan x="15">Barefoot Landing</tspan></text><text class="m" x="15" y="12.5">about 11 min</text></g></g><g transform="translate(213.3 198.3)"><g class="k"><g transform="scale(0.8)"><ellipse cx="0" cy="1" rx="7" ry="2.4" fill="#1c2028" opacity=".18"/><path d="M0 0C-3-6-13-14-13-26a13 13 0 1 1 26 0c0 12-10 20-13 26z" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.5"/><use href="#c3r-main-street-home" x="-8.5" y="-34.5" width="17" height="17" color="#ffffff"/></g><text class="h" x="-15" y="-14.5" text-anchor="end"><tspan x="-15">Main Street</tspan></text></g></g></g></svg></div><figcaption>Drive times by car from Main Street at Ocean Drive, without traffic. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices">What do homes cost in North Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical resold house in North Myrtle Beach sold for about $565,000 in the past year; half sold between about $420,000 and $740,000. A condo sold for about $310,000, and a new house from a builder for about $440,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Condos sell for about the same in every part along the ocean, about $310,000 to $360,000. Houses differ by part far more. More than half the homes sold here in the past year went to a buyer whose tax bill goes to another state.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Homes for sale now</h3><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes for sale in North Myrtle Beach at the last count"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes for sale in North Myrtle Beach at the last count</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Kind, for sale</span><span role="columnheader">Middle asking price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 250 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$690,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Townhouses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">35 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.473" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$330,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condos</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 570 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.433" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$300,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Manufactured homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">39 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.209" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$145,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Asking prices, not sales. Listing counts from the Coastal Carolinas Association of REALTORS MLS, in aggregate.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On November 3, 2026, about 250 houses and 575 condos were for sale in the city. Ask us to run the count again for the part you like.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Know what a house is worth before you offer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. An agent pulls what nearby homes like it sold for in the past year and tells you what the house is worth, with those sales behind it.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us value a house</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flood"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood zone">Does North Myrtle Beach flood?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 1 in 3 homes in North Myrtle Beach is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, more of them condos than houses. The part you choose decides most of it.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, by part of North Myrtle Beach"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, by part of North Myrtle Beach</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part, houses and condos</span><span role="columnheader">All homes</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Cherry Grove</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">houses 95%, condos 84%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.881" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">88%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Windy Hill</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">houses 17%, condos 71%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.542" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">54%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Ocean Drive</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">houses 10%, condos 68%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.523" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">52%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Tilghman Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">houses 15%, condos 42%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.329" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">33%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Little River Neck</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">houses 13%, condos 10%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.099" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">10%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Crescent Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">houses 1%, condos 15%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.098" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">10%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of US 17</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">houses 5%, condos 10%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.068" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">7%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Across the waterway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">of about 5,200</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">2 homes</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Every home in the county's parcel records, tested against FEMA's flood map as the county carries it.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The high-risk zone has two kinds here. The VE zone is the oceanfront, where storm waves add to the flood; the A zones are the rest of it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do you need flood insurance in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A federally regulated lender must require flood insurance when the building is in FEMA's high-risk zone, and any lender can ask for it elsewhere. In ZIP code 29582, which covers most of the city, a federal flood policy on a house usually cost:</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>A federal flood policy on a house in ZIP code 29582</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Where the house is</th><th scope="col">A year, at the middle</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Outside the flood zone</th><td data-label="A year, at the middle">About $600</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">In the flood zone, back from the ocean (A zone)</th><td data-label="A year, at the middle">About $1,460</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">In the flood zone on the oceanfront, where waves reach (VE zone)</th><td data-label="A year, at the middle">About $2,150</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A new policy takes effect 30 days after you apply and pay; it can start sooner when you buy it with your home loan.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside the zone is not the same as never flooded. Our page on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how to find out if a house flooded</a> shows every record we use, and our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance page</a> explains each policy.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Find out a house's flood risk before you offer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We check its flood zone, its elevation and its flood history, and tell you whether a lender must require flood insurance.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check a house's flood zone</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does a home in North Myrtle Beach cost to own each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical house you live in costs about $8,400 a year to own, before any mortgage. A typical condo costs more, about $11,000, because of the condo fee.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Each year, as your home, before any mortgage</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">What you pay</th><th scope="col">House, about $565,000</th><th scope="col">Condo, about $310,000</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Property tax</th><td data-label="House, about $565,000">About $2,500</td><td data-label="Condo, about $310,000">About $1,400</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Home insurance</th><td data-label="House, about $565,000">About $2,000</td><td data-label="Condo, about $310,000">About $800</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Flood policy, outside the flood zone</th><td data-label="House, about $565,000">About $600</td><td data-label="Condo, about $310,000">Not counted</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">HOA or condo fee</th><td data-label="House, about $565,000">None on about half</td><td data-label="Condo, about $310,000">About $8,400</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Upkeep</th><td data-label="House, about $565,000">About $3,300</td><td data-label="Condo, about $310,000">About $700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Together</th><td data-label="House, about $565,000">About $8,400</td><td data-label="Condo, about $310,000">About $11,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">As a second home or rental, the tax is three times as much. The house then costs about $13,000 a year and the condo about $14,000, if the other costs stay the same.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tax is on the county's value of the home, and a sale resets that value toward the price you pay. You must apply for the lower rate on a home you live in; our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax page</a> shows how.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where the other figures come from</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Home insurance is the middle that Horry County owners pay for a house they live in; half pay between about $1,300 and $3,000. On the beach side of US 17, an insurer may leave wind and hail out of a policy. The owner can then buy that cover separately, for example from the state's wind and hail association.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The condo fee is the middle fee of condos for sale in ZIP code 29582, about $700 a month. It may also pay the insurance on the shared building. About half the houses for sale in that ZIP code list no HOA fee.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Upkeep is the average owners spend a year in the South Atlantic states. If you buy with us, we get you an insurance quote for the address before you make an offer. Our <a href="/buyers/cost-to-own/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">cost to own page</a> compares the towns nearby.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="renting"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting it out">Can you rent out a home by the night in North Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, with a city business license. Every short-term rental in the city needs one, renewed each year, and must collect lodging taxes. The city has no special zoning or rental permit beyond the license.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An HOA or the deed can still bar rentals, and we read the HOA's rules and the deed before you offer. A rental owner here has five things to get right:</p><ol class="c3-nmb-steps"><li><strong>The license.</strong> A city business license, renewed every year.</li><li><strong>The parking number.</strong> When you apply or renew, you report the parking spaces on the property's own land. That number is the most cars guests can park there. It goes in every ad and rental agreement and is posted inside. Where an HOA or the deed limits parking, the owner certifies the number matches.</li><li><strong>The lodging taxes.</strong> Guests pay 12 percent on a stay under 90 days, split between the state, the city and the county.</li><li><strong>The trash days.</strong> The city collects a rental's trash on its regular day plus Friday, Saturday and Sunday. Recycling goes out only on the regular day.</li><li><strong>The quiet hours.</strong> They run from 11 p.m. to 7 a.m., and fireworks are banned everywhere in the city, with a $310 ticket for a first offense.</li></ol><div class="c3-nmb-ex"><strong>Example.</strong> On a $2,000 week, a guest pays about $240 in lodging taxes, which the owner collects and pays to the state, the city and the county.</div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is North Myrtle Beach changing its rental rules?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city has held workshops and public sessions on possible new short-term rental rules. Its rental page lists no new rental ordinance adopted, and the license rule is the one in force. Earlier tries, a moratorium on large rental houses and a draft ordinance, failed.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our pages on <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules by town</a>, <a href="/invest/accommodations-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">filing the lodging taxes</a> and <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what a nightly rental earns</a> go further.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Know a building's rental rules before you offer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the condo or the house. We read the HOA's rules and the deed for rental limits, and count the parking spaces the city will ask for.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us read the rental rules</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="pros-and-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in North Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The good points are the beach, the water, the golf and the choice of parts. The hard ones are the flood zone at the north end, the condo fees, and how few houses by the ocean are main homes.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>About nine miles of beach, Main Street at Ocean Drive, and the marsh parks and boat ramp at Cherry Grove.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Houses on the Cherry Grove channels, with water behind the house.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Four golf courses at Barefoot Resort, across the waterway.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Almost no flood zone across the waterway, and about 7 in 100 homes west of US 17.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Cherry Grove is almost all in the high-risk flood zone, and its flood policies cost more. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the flood zone, the elevation and the flood history before you offer.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Most houses by the ocean are second homes or rentals, and fewer neighbors live there all year. <span class="c3-pc-do">Inland, about 3 in 4 houses are the owner's main home.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Condo fees are high: the middle condo for sale lists about $700 a month. <span class="c3-pc-do">We read the condo's budget and rules before you offer.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Summer traffic on US 17 slows every drive. <span class="c3-pc-do">We time the drives from any house you like.</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="north-myrtle-beach-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">North Myrtle Beach FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is North Myrtle Beach part of Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. North Myrtle Beach is its own city in Horry County, South Carolina. Four beach towns joined to form it in 1968, and it has its own city tax and rental rules. The Myrtle Beach oceanfront is about 30 minutes south by car.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What are the sections of North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The four old beach towns are Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach and Windy Hill. Tilghman Beach, Little River Neck, the mainland west of US 17 and the neighborhoods across the waterway make eight parts.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you drive a golf cart in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, from sunrise to sunset, on city streets posted 35 mph or less, with a state permit sticker from the DMV and a licensed driver. A cart may cross Ocean Boulevard, 27th Avenue South, US 17 and Sea Mountain Highway, but not drive along them.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are dogs allowed on the beach in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, on a leash. From May 15 to Labor Day they must be off the beach from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. In that season the beach takes umbrellas only, no tents or canopies.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What does it cost to own a home in North Myrtle Beach each year?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">As your home, before any mortgage, about $8,400 for a typical house and about $11,000 for a typical condo. That covers tax, insurance, a flood policy outside the zone, the condo fee and upkeep.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On a house the county values at $565,000, about $2,500 a year as your home and about $7,500 as a second home or rental.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is North Myrtle Beach safe?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. We pull the reported crime figures for the area around any house you ask about.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which schools serve North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County Schools assigns schools by address. North Myrtle Beach is one of its nine attendance areas, with North Myrtle Beach High School, North Myrtle Beach Middle School and Ocean Drive Elementary. We look up the assigned schools for any house you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/profile/North_Myrtle_Beach_city,_South_Carolina?g=160XX00US4551280" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census profile</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood policies</a>, <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-44/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-64/section-64.3" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">44 CFR 64.3</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 USC 4012a</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t01c001.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 1-1-665</a>, <a href="https://www.scencyclopedia.org/sce/entries/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Encyclopedia</a>, <a href="https://www.barefootgolf.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Barefoot Resort golf</a>, <a href="https://www.parks.nmb.us/833/Short-term-Rentals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city rental page</a>, <a href="https://www.parks.nmb.us/DocumentCenter/View/5580/Short-term-Rental-Rules" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city rental rules</a>, <a href="https://www.parks.nmb.us/249/Beach-Laws" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">beach laws</a>, <a href="https://www.parks.nmb.us/600/Golf-Cart-Laws" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">golf cart laws</a>, <a href="https://www.parks.nmb.us/473/Parks" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city parks</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/tax/accommodations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">lodging taxes</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountyschools.net/about-hcs/our-schools" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Schools</a>. Our counts from county records and CCMLS listings; the parts are ours. Insurance: Census ACS. Upkeep: Census AHS.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Cherry Grove and its pier from a height. Photo: Melikamp, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cherry_Grove_Pier.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the photo and cut square, 4:3 and 16:9 crops from its center.</div><div role="listitem">Houses on the Cherry Grove channels, from above. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USGS The National Map</a>. Chapter3 Realty exported this view from the NAIP image service, raised the contrast a little and added labels placed from OpenStreetMap, Horry County and Census coordinates.</div><div role="listitem">Tilghman Beach, from above. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USGS The National Map</a>. Chapter3 Realty exported this view from the NAIP image service, raised the contrast a little and added labels placed from OpenStreetMap, Horry County and Census coordinates.</div><div role="listitem">Ocean Drive and Main Street, from above. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USGS The National Map</a>. Chapter3 Realty exported this view from the NAIP image service, raised the contrast a little and added labels placed from OpenStreetMap, Horry County and Census coordinates.</div><div role="listitem">The pavilion at Ocean Drive Beach, on a postcard. Photo: Tichnor Brothers, Boston (publisher), <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-US-no_notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ocean_Drive_Beach_-_Roberts_Pavilion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the scan.</div><div role="listitem">Atlantic Beach between Crescent Beach and Windy Hill, from above. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" r